#: css/avatar.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`.instui-avatar` · <span class=\"instui-pill -color-success pantoken-doc-tag\">stable</span> — A user avatar showing initials or an image, circular by default."
msgstr "`.instui-avatar` · <span class=\"instui-pill -color-success pantoken-doc-tag\">stable</span> — He āhua kaiwhakamahi e whakaatu ana i ngā tauākī tuatahi, i tētahi whakaahua rānei, ā, porowhita te āhua mā te taunoa."

#: css/avatar.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "By default the palette colour tints the initials on a transparent surface; `-has-inverse-color` fills the surface with the colour and puts the initials on-colour. The `-color-ai` variant always fills with the violet→sea gradient. For a full display name, put it in the content (so it stays in the accessibility tree) and add `data-initials=\"XX\"` for the compact visual — the real text is what a screen reader announces. Without `data-initials`, overflowing content just hard-clips (no ellipsis); wrap it in `.name` for a precise single-leading-letter clip instead, or split it into `.first-name`/`.last-name` for two clipped letters (either half can be omitted and the other stays centred)."
msgstr "I te taunoa, ka tāia e te kara o te pae ngā tauākī tuatahi i runga i tētahi mata māwhero; ka kīia te mata e `-has-inverse-color` ki te kara ka tūnga ngā tauākī tuatahi i runga tonu i te kara. Ko te rerekētanga `-color-ai` ka kī tonu ki te āputa kōkō-rori → moana. Mō te ingoa whakaatu katoa, whakanohoia ki roto i te ihirangi (kia noho tonu i te rākau uru) ā, tāpirihia `data-initials=\"XX\"` mō te āhua pūnoa — ko te tuhinga tūturu te mea ka pānuitia e te kaipānui mata. Mēnā kāore he `data-initials`, ka tapahia pakari noa te ihirangi (kāore he tohu elipsi); ā, tīpakohia te whakakī i roto i `.name` mō te tapahi tika ki te reta mātāmua anake, rānei whakatotoria ki roto i `.first-name`/`.last-name` mō ngā reta e rua kua tapahia (ka taea te whakakāore i tētahi o ngā haurua, ā, ka noho te tētahi i te pokapū)."

