msgid "A weekday column header."
msgstr "He taitara kolamu mō te rā o te wiki."

#: css/callout.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: callout"
msgstr ""

#: css/callout.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`div[class~=\"instui-callout\"]` — Inline information alert for a short reminder or note."
msgstr "`div[class~=\"instui-callout\"]` — Ahu whakamōhio whakauru mō te whakamaharatanga poto, mō te tuhipoka."

#: css/callout.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "✅ Use Callout when:"
msgstr "✅ Whakamahia te Callout ina:"

#: css/callout.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- You need to highlight important information or reminders inline\n- The message is relatively brief (a sentence to a short paragraph)\n- The alert should draw attention without interrupting the main flow\n🚫 Don't use Callout when:"
msgstr "- Me whakaahua koe i ngā mōhiohio nui, ngā whakamaharatanga rānei i roto i te tuhinga\n- He poto te karere (he rerenga kōrero, he parakaraka poto rānei)\n- Me akiaki te whakamōhio i te aro atu, kaua e aukati i te rere o te ihirangi matua\n🚫 Kaua e whakamahi i te Callout ina:"

#: css/callout.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- The message requires interaction or multiple actions — use a Modal or Alert Dialog\n- The content is the main focus of the page — use a Card or Hero layout instead"
msgstr "- Me whakawhitiwhiti, me mahi-rua ngā mahi — whakamahia he Modal, he Alert Dialog rānei\n- Ko te ihirangi te pokapū matua o te whārangi — whakamahia he Card, he Hero layout rānei"

#: css/callout.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- Ensure the alert role is properly applied (role=\"alert\" or role=\"status\")\n- Use semantic color contrast that meets WCAG AA standards\n- Don't rely on color alone to convey meaning"
msgstr "- Ensure the alert role is properly applied (role=\"alert\" or role=\"status\")\n- Whakamahia ngā tae mōhio ā-tūturu me te rerekētanga e tutuki ana i ngā paerewa WCAG AA\n- Kaua e whakawhirinaki ki te tae anake ki te tuku i te tikanga"

#: css/callout.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Alert message content"
msgstr "Ihirangi karere whakamōhio"

#: css/callout.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Container for the text content."
msgstr "Ipu mō te ihirangi kuputuhi."

#: css/callout.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Optional icon to the left of the content."
msgstr "He tohu kōwhiringa kei te taha mauī o te ihirangi."

#: css/card.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: card"
msgstr ""

#: css/card.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`.instui-card` — A surface container that accepts arbitrary content."
msgstr "`.instui-card` — He ipu mata e whakaae ana i ngā ihirangi huhua."

#: css/card.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "**Variant** controls how direct children are styled: `content` (default) leaves them\n  unstyled; `container` stacks them as bordered, padded sections. Padding scales with\n  viewport width and is the same across both variants.\n  **Size** is fully responsive — padding and border-radius step up automatically at 320px\n  (20rem) and 640px (40rem) via standard `min-width` media queries; no size class is needed.\n  Pair with `@pantoken/components` for heading, button, and other inline components."
msgstr "**Variant** e whakahaere ana i te āhua o ngā tamariki tūhono: `content` (taunoa) ka waiho kia kore-āhua; `container` ka tūhono hei wāhanga ā-āraitanga, ā-kapi. Ka pīkau te whakakī ki te whānuitanga o te mata, ā, he ōrite i ngā variant e rua.\n  Ko te **Rahi** he tino urutau — ka piki aunoa te whakakī me te poro-ā-ārai i te 320px (20rem) me te 640px (40rem) mā ngā pātai pāpāho paerewa `min-width`; kāore he karaehe-rahi e hiahiatia. Tautokohia ki `@pantoken/components` mō ngā taitara, pātene, me ētahi atu wāhanga ā-raina."

#: css/card.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Use `<article>` as the card element when the card is a self-contained unit of content;\n  use `<section>` when grouped within a larger landmark. In `-variant-container`, prefer\n  `<section>` elements as direct children so each bordered region carries semantic meaning."
msgstr "Whakamahia `<article>` hei waahanga kāri mēnā ko te kāri he wāhanga ihirangi motuhake; whakamahia `<section>` mēnā ka rōpūhia i roto i tētahi tohu nui ake. I roto i `-variant-container`, me pai ake te whakamahi i ngā waahanga `<section>` hei tamariki tūhono kia ia rohe ā-āraitanga ka mau i tētahi tikanga pūāhua."

#: css/card.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Content card -nocard"
msgstr "Kāri ihirangi -nocard"

#: css/card.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Container card -nocard"
msgstr "Kāri ipu -nocard"

#: css/card.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Container card; direct children become bordered, padded sections."
msgstr "Kāri ipu; ka huri ngā tamariki tūhono hei wāhanga ā-āraitanga, ā-kapi."

#: css/card.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Standard content card; children are unstyled. Default when no variant is set."
msgstr "Kāri ihirangi paerewa; kāore i whakapaehia ngā tamariki. Koinei te taunoa mēnā kāore he variant kua tautuhia."

#: css/card.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- `@scope` is Baseline 2023 Newly Available; the card degrades to an unscoped flat stylesheet\n  in older browsers with no loss of visible styling."
msgstr "- `@scope` is Baseline 2023 Newly Available; ka heke te kāri ki tētahi anga kāraka papa kore-ā-rohe i ngā pūtirotiro tawhito, kāore he ngaro o te āhua e kitea ana."

#: css/card.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- [heading](/api/css/heading.md) — Place directly in the card or inside a container section.\n- [button](/api/css/button.md) — Place directly in the card or inside a container section.\n- [img](/api/css/img.md) — Place directly in the card as a media region.\n- [badge](/api/css/badge.md) — Place directly in the card as a status indicator."
msgstr "- [heading](/api/css/heading.md) — Whakanoho tika ki roto i te kāri, ki roto rānei i tētahi wāhanga ipu.\n- [button](/api/css/button.md) — Whakanoho tika ki roto i te kāri, ki roto rānei i tētahi wāhanga ipu.\n- [img](/api/css/img.md) — Whakanoho tika ki roto i te kāri hei rohe pāpāho.\n- [badge](/api/css/badge.md) — Whakanoho tika ki roto i te kāri hei tohu tūnga."

#: css/card.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- https://drafts.csswg.org/css-cascade-6/#scoping"
msgstr "- https://drafts.csswg.org/css-cascade-6/#scoping"

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: checkbox"
msgstr ""

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`.instui-checkbox` — A native checkbox and its label, or a switch via `-variant-toggle`."
msgstr "`.instui-checkbox` — He pouaka tohu taketake me tōna tapanga, rānei he pana mā te `-variant-toggle`."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Set `el.indeterminate = true` in JavaScript to show the mixed-state dash; the checked tick auto-contrasts against the fill — white on a dark fill, near-black on a light one. Also sets its own `gap` between the control and its label; chaining a `-gap-*` spacing utility modifier overrides that built-in value."
msgstr "Tautuhia `el.indeterminate = true` i roto i te JavaScript kia whakaatu i te rārangi āhua-mix; ka whakatairite aunoa te tohu kua tīpakohia ki te kapi — mā i runga i te kapi pouri, tata-pango i runga i te kapi māmā. Ka tautuhia hoki tōna ake `gap` i waenganui i te whakahaere me tana tapanga; mā te here i tētahi kaitahuri wāhī `-gap-*` ka whakakapi i taua uara ā-roto."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "**Source:** [checkbox.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/checkbox/checkbox.css)"
msgstr "**Source:** [checkbox.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/checkbox/checkbox.css)"

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A native `<input type=\"checkbox\">` drives `:checked`, `:indeterminate`, and `:disabled`; set `el.indeterminate = true` in JavaScript for the mixed state, and note that `-readonly` is styling only since checkboxes have no native readonly attribute."
msgstr "He `<input type=\"checkbox\">` taketake e tarai i ngā `:checked`, `:indeterminate`, me `:disabled`; tautuhia `el.indeterminate = true` i roto i te JavaScript mō te āhua-mix, ā, kia mōhiotia kātahi hoki ko `-readonly` he āhua ā-tae anake nō te mea kāore ngā pouaka tohu he āhuatanga pānui-anake ā-taketake."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Invalid (error) state."
msgstr "Āhua hē (tapae)."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Place the label after the control."
msgstr "Whakauruhia te tapanga i muri i te whakahaere."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Place the label before the control."
msgstr "Whakauruhia te tapanga i mua i te whakahaere."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Place the label above the control."
msgstr "Whakauruhia te tapanga i runga ake i te whakahaere."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Read-only state."
msgstr "Āhua pānui-anake."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Show the required-field asterisk next to the label."
msgstr "Whakaatu te asterisk mō te mara e hiahiatia ana i te taha o te tapanga."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Render as a switch instead of a box."
msgstr "Whakaatu hei pana, kaua hei pouaka."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The required-field asterisk."
msgstr "Te asterisk mō te mara e hiahiatia ana."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "On `-variant-toggle`, the state glyph riding the handle: an X when off, a check when on."
msgstr "I runga i te `-variant-toggle`, ko te tohu āhua e noho ana i runga i te kakau: he X ina kāore, he tohu-tika ina kei runga."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The masked tick or dash glyph centered in the box; on `-variant-toggle` it becomes the sliding handle instead."
msgstr "Te tohu huna (tohu-tika rānei te rārangi) kei waenganui i te pouaka; i runga i te `-variant-toggle` ka noho hei kakau tāheke hurihuri."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The box's mask glyph: a tick when checked, a dash when indeterminate."
msgstr "Te tohu kapi o te pouaka: he tohu-tika ina kua tīpakohia, he rārangi ina kāore i te mārama."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The toggle border width."
msgstr "Te whānui ārai o te pana."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The toggle switch height."
msgstr "Te teitei o te pana tāheke."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The computed handle diameter."
msgstr "Te diamita kua tātai o te kakau."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The handle inset from each track edge."
msgstr "Te whakawhiu o te kakau mai i ia taha o te ara."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The toggle track width."
msgstr "Te whānui o te ara pana."

#: css/checkbox.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- [radio](/api/css/radio.md) — The single-select counterpart."
msgstr "- [radio](/api/css/radio.md) — Te hoa mō te kōwhiringa kotahi."

#: css/close-button.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: close-button"
msgstr ""

#: css/close-button.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`.instui-close-button` — A transparent icon button that draws its own × glyph, in three sizes plus an on-color variant."
msgstr "`.instui-close-button` — He pātene tohu mārama e tuhi ana i tana ake tohu ×, i roto i ngā rahi e toru me tētahi rerekētanga ā-tea."

#: css/close-button.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Always renders as an icon-only control with no visible label, so an `aria-label` is required, not optional; compare to `button`'s `-without-background` ghost variant, which keeps a text label."
msgstr "Ka whakaatuhia i ngā wā katoa hei mana tohu-anake, kāore he tapanga kitea; nō reira me whai `aria-label` — ehara i te kōwhiringa; whakaritea ki te rerekētanga 'ghost' `-without-background` o `button`, e pupuri ana i tētahi tapanga kuputuhi."

#: css/close-button.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "**Source:** [close-button.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/close-button/close-button.css)"
msgstr "**Source:** [close-button.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/close-button/close-button.css)"

#: css/close-button.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Give the icon-only button an `aria-label` (e.g. \"Close\"), and mark a disabled button with `aria-disabled` (or the native `disabled`)."
msgstr "Hoatu tētahi `aria-label` ki te pātene tohu-anake (hei tauira: \"Katia\"), ā, tohuhia te pātene kua mono mā te whakamahi i te `aria-disabled` (rānei te `disabled` taketake)."

#: css/close-button.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "For a close button placed on a coloured (non-neutral) surface."
msgstr "Mō tētahi pātene kati ka whakanohoia ki runga i tētahi mata tae (kāore i te tauwhāiti)."

#: css/close-button.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The × glyph, masked in `currentColor`."
msgstr "Te tohu ×, kua ārai i roto i `currentColor`."

#: css/close-button.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- [button](/api/css/button.md) — The general-purpose action button."
msgstr "- [button](/api/css/button.md) — Te pātene mahi whānui."

#: css/color.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: color"
msgstr ""

#: css/color.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`.--text-danger` — Semantic colour utilities: `.--bg-<name>`, `.--text-<name>` (aliased as `.--color-<name>`), and `.--border-<name>` for the curated semantic palette. Every one of these also has a component-attached alias modifier (for example `-bg-danger` on any `.instui-<component>`)."
msgstr "`.--text-danger` — Ngā taputapu tae ā-tikanga: `.--bg-<name>`, `.--text-<name>` (taurite ki `.--color-<name>`), me `.--border-<name>` mō te karaehe ā-tikanga kua tīpakohia. Ia o ēnei he whakarerekētanga ingoa taurite e hono ana ki tētahi wāhanga (hei tauira `-bg-danger` i runga i tētahi `.instui-<component>`)."

#: css/color.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "**Source:** [generate.ts](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/scripts/generate.ts)"
msgstr "**Source:** [generate.ts](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/scripts/generate.ts)"

#: css/color.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Applies the semantic danger text colour."
msgstr "Ka whakatauhia te tae kuputuhi tūraru ā-tikanga."

#: css/color.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Background colour utilities for semantic and component-aligned names."
msgstr "Ngā taputapu tae papamuri mō ngā ingoa ā-tikanga me ngā ingoa e hāngai ana ki ngā wahanga."

#: css/color.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Border colour utilities for semantic and component-aligned names."
msgstr "Ngā taputapu tae tapawhā mō ngā ingoa ā-tikanga me ngā ingoa e hāngai ana ki ngā wahanga."

#: css/color.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Alias of `--text-*` for text colour utilities."
msgstr "He ingoa taurite o `--text-*` mō ngā taputapu tae kuputuhi."

#: css/color.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Text colour utilities for semantic and component-aligned names."
msgstr "Ngā taputapu tae kuputuhi mō ngā ingoa ā-tikanga me ngā ingoa e hāngai ana ki ngā wahanga."

#: css/context-view.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: context-view"
msgstr ""

#: css/context-view.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`.instui-context-view` — An elevated callout with a caret, positionable on any side; works as a native `[popover]`."
msgstr "`.instui-context-view` — He whakamārama whakaarahi me te caret, ka taea te tu ki tetahi taha; e mahi ana pērā i te `[popover]` taketake."

#: css/context-view.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The caret is two stacked `::before`/`::after` triangles (border then fill) so it reads correctly against a matching surface; as a `[popover]` it needs the same open/`popovertarget` wiring as `popover`, but unlike `tooltip`, it dismisses on outside click or Escape."
msgstr "Ko te caret he rua ngā tapatoru `::before`/`::after` kua whakakāhoretia (tuakana, katahi ko te kapi) kia tika te pānui ki runga i tētahi mata hei hāngai; hei `[popover]` ia e hiahiatia ana ngā hononga open/`popovertarget` me taua āhua pērā i te `popover`, engari, kāore pēnei i te `tooltip` — ka whakamutu rānei i te pāwhiri ki waho, i te pāwhiri Escape rānei."

#: css/context-view.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "**Source:** [context-view.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/context-view/context-view.css)"
msgstr "**Source:** [context-view.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/context-view/context-view.css)"

#: css/context-view.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Dark (inverse) colour scheme."
msgstr "Ahu tae pouri (huri)."

#: css/context-view.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Sit below the anchor."
msgstr "Noho i raro i te hono."

#: css/context-view.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Sit at the end (inline-end) of the anchor."
msgstr "Noho i te mutunga (inline-end) o te hono."

#: css/context-view.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Sit at the start (inline-start) of the anchor."
msgstr "Noho i te tīmatanga (inline-start) o te hono."

#: css/context-view.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Sit above the anchor."
msgstr "Noho i runga ake o te hono."

#: css/context-view.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Renders the caret's inner fill triangle."
msgstr "E whakaatu ana i te tapatoru whakakī o roto o te caret."

#: css/context-view.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Renders the caret's outer border triangle."
msgstr "E whakaatu ana i te tapatoru ārai o waho o te caret."

#: css/context-view.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- Uses CSS anchor positioning (`position-anchor`, `position-area`, `position-try-fallbacks`) and the native `[popover]` API behind an `@supports` guard; needs a recent Chromium or Safari, and falls back to a UA-centred popover elsewhere."
msgstr "- Ka whakamahi i te tūranga hono CSS (`position-anchor`, `position-area`, `position-try-fallbacks`) me te API taketake `[popover]` i muri i tētahi kaitiaki `@supports`; e hiahiatia ana he Chromium hou ranei he Safari, ā, ka huri ki tētahi popover e aro ana ki te UA i ērā atu wāhi."

#: css/context-view.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- [popover](/api/css/popover.md) — The generic top-layer popover.\n- [tooltip](/api/css/tooltip.md) — A smaller hover or focus callout."
msgstr "- [popover](/api/css/popover.md) — Te popover whānui mō te paparanga o runga.\n- [tooltip](/api/css/tooltip.md) — He whakamārama iti mō te hover, mō te aro."

#: css/cursor.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: cursor"
msgstr ""

#: css/cursor.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`.--cursor-pointer` — `cursor` as a composable, global class — `.--cursor-<value>` — usable bare or chained onto any component (`.instui-button.--cursor-pointer`)."
msgstr "`.--cursor-pointer` — `cursor` hei akomanga hanga-apiti, ā-ao — `.--cursor-<value>` — ka taea te whakamahi mā te waiho kē, mā te hono rānei ki runga i tētahi wahanga (`.instui-button.--cursor-pointer`)."

#: css/cursor.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "**Source:** [index.ts](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/utilities/cursor/index.ts)"
msgstr "**Source:** [index.ts](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/utilities/cursor/index.ts)"

