#: css/drawer-layout.content.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: drawer-layout.content"
msgstr "# CSS: drawer-layout.content"

#: css/drawer-layout.content.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`.content` — The primary content pane that fills remaining space beside the tray."
msgstr "`.content` — Ko te paewhiri ihirangi matua e whakakī ana i te waahi e toe ana i te taha o te paewhiri."

#: css/drawer-layout.content.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Once the parent's inline-size drops below `46em` (`16em` tray width + `30em` breakpoint), a `@container` query on the parent's `pantoken-drawer-layout` container drops this member's `min-inline-size` to `0` automatically, matching the manual `[should-overlay-tray]` override."
msgstr "Ka tino whakaitihia te rahi ā-ipurangi (inline-size) o te mātua ki raro ake i te `46em` (`16em` whanui o te paewhiri + `30em` wā whatunga), ā, ka whiwhi te pātai `@container` i runga i te ipu `pantoken-drawer-layout` o te mātua i te whakaheke aunoa i te `min-inline-size` o tēnei mema ki `0`, e ōrite ana ki te whakakapi ā-ringa `[should-overlay-tray]`."

#: css/drawer-layout.content.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Carry `role=\"region\"` (InstUI's DrawerLayout convention) and name it with `aria-label`/`aria-labelledby` when context alone doesn't identify it."
msgstr "Puritia te `role=\"region\"` (te tikanga DrawerLayout a InstUI) ā, ingoaia kia whakamahi i te `aria-label`/`aria-labelledby` mēnā kāore te horopaki anake e tautuhi."

#: css/drawer-layout.content.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- [drawer-layout.tray](/api/css/drawer-layout.tray.md) — The adjacent panel in the same flex row."
msgstr "- [drawer-layout.tray](/mi/api/css/drawer-layout.tray.md) — The adjacent panel in the same flex row."

#: css/drawer-layout.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: drawer-layout"
msgstr ""

#: css/drawer-layout.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`.instui-drawer-layout` — A split layout with a collapsible side tray and a primary scrollable content pane."
msgstr "`.instui-drawer-layout` — He tatauranga wehe me tētahi karu taha e taea te tōkia, me tētahi pane ihirangi matua e taea te kauhau."

#: css/drawer-layout.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`-placement-end` and the default (start) both use `flex-direction`/`inset-inline-*` logical properties, not `left`/`right`, so the tray's side follows `direction`/`dir=\"rtl\"` automatically — no separate RTL rules are needed."
msgstr "`-placement-end` me te taunoa (tīmatanga) e whakamahi ana i ngā rawa arorau `flex-direction`/`inset-inline-*`, kāore i te `left`/`right`, nō reira ka ū te taha o te karu ki `direction`/`dir=\"rtl\"` āwhina āunoa — kāore he ture RTL motuhake e hiahiatia."

#: css/drawer-layout.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "**Source:** [drawer-layout.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/drawer-layout/drawer-layout.css)"
msgstr "**Source:** [drawer-layout.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/drawer-layout/drawer-layout.css)"

#: css/drawer-layout.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "When the tray acts as navigation, label it with an accessible heading or `aria-label`. Give `.content` `role=\"region\"` (InstUI's DrawerLayout convention) and name it with `aria-label`/`aria-labelledby` when context alone doesn't identify it."
msgstr "A, ina mahi te karu hei aratohu, tapaina me tētahi taitara قابل-ikotahi (accessible heading) rānei `aria-label`. Homai `.content` `role=\"region\"` (tūāhua DrawerLayout o InstUI) ka tapaina mā `aria-label`/`aria-labelledby` mēnā kāore te horopaki anake e tautohu i tōna ingoa."

#: css/drawer-layout.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Show the tray even when the `open` attribute is absent."
msgstr "Whakaaturia te karu ahakoa kāore te āhuatanga `open` i te wātea."

#: css/drawer-layout.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Dock the tray on the inline-end side."
msgstr "Tūhia te karu ki te taha mutunga-ā-ipurangi (inline-end)."

#: css/drawer-layout.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Dock the tray on the inline-start side (the default; sets it explicitly)."
msgstr "Tūhia te karu ki te taha tīmatanga-ā-ipurangi (inline-start) (te taunoa; whakaūhia ēnei tautuhinga)."

#: css/drawer-layout.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "<span class=\"instui-pill pantoken-doc-tag pantoken-doc-tag-interaction\">Interaction</span> — Render the tray as an overlay instead of shrinking content inline."
msgstr ""

#: css/drawer-layout.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The main pane."
msgstr "Te pane matua."

#: css/drawer-layout.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The side panel."
msgstr "Te panui taha."

#: css/drawer-layout.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Width threshold for overlay mode (`30em`, themed via responsive utilities)."
msgstr "Te whārite whānui mō te aratau uhi (overlay) (`30em`, ātathemehia mā ngā taputapu urupare)."

#: css/drawer-layout.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- The `drawer-layout.tray`/`drawer-layout.content` members switch to overlay mode automatically via a `@container` query once this element's inline-size drops below tray-width + `--pantoken-bp-md`. The `@pantoken/interactions` behavior additionally toggles `[should-overlay-tray]`/`.-should-overlay-tray` (a manual override) and emits `overlaytraychange` for apps that need the change as an event."
msgstr "- Ka hurihia āunoa ngā mema `drawer-layout.tray`/`drawer-layout.content` ki te aratau uhi mā te pātai `@container` mēnā ka iti haere te rahi-ipurangi o tēnei tūemi ki raro i te whānui-karu + `--pantoken-bp-md`. Ka huri anō te whanonga `@pantoken/interactions` i te `[should-overlay-tray]`/`.-should-overlay-tray` (he whakakāinga ā-ringa) ā, ka whakaputa i `overlaytraychange` mō ngā taupānga e hiahiatia ana te whakarerekētanga hei kaupapa (event)."

#: css/drawer-layout.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- [tray](/api/css/tray.md) — A standalone edge overlay; this layout keeps tray and content in the same flow.\n- [context-view](/api/css/context-view.md) — A smaller anchored surface for contextual actions and detail."
msgstr "- [tray](/api/css/tray.md) — He uhi taha motuhake; ka mau tonu tēnei tatauranga i te karu me te ihirangi i roto i te rōpū kotahi.\n- [context-view](/api/css/context-view.md) — He mata whakanoho iti mō ngā mahi horopaki me ngā taipitopito."

#: css/drawer-layout.tray.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: drawer-layout.tray"
msgstr ""

#: css/drawer-layout.tray.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`.tray` — The side panel beside main content, with optional overlay and tray-like surface modifiers."
msgstr "`.tray` — He papa taha i te taha o te ihirangi matua, me ngā whakarerekētanga kōwhiringa pērā i te ūru (overlay) me ngā mata rite-ipu (tray-like)."

#: css/drawer-layout.tray.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Positioning uses `inset-inline-start`/`inset-inline` (never `left`/`right`), so `-placement-end` docks to the true trailing edge in both LTR and RTL."
msgstr "Ko te tūnga e whakamahi ana i `inset-inline-start`/`inset-inline` (kāore e whakamahi i `left`/`right`), nō reira ka taurite a `-placement-end` ki te pito hiku tūturu i roto i te LTR me te RTL."

#: css/drawer-layout.tray.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "If used as navigation, wrap links in a semantic `<nav>` and provide an accessible name."
msgstr "Mēnā ka whakamahia hei whakatere (navigation), whakawhiwhia ngā hononga ki roto i tētahi `<nav>` ā-tikanga, ā, hoatu he ingoa e taea te uru ai ki te katoa."

#: css/drawer-layout.tray.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Dock this tray to inline-end when overlay mode is active."
msgstr "Tautokohia tēnei rīhi ki te inline-end ina kua whakahoatuhia te aratau ūru (overlay)."

#: css/drawer-layout.tray.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Remove the panel edge border."
msgstr "Tangohia te tāpare (border) o te mata o te panui."

#: css/drawer-layout.tray.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Remove elevation when overlay mode is active."
msgstr "Whakaitia te pikinga (elevation) ina whakahoatuhia te aratau ūru (overlay)."

#: css/drawer-layout.tray.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- [drawer-layout.content](/api/css/drawer-layout.content.md) — The primary pane that flexes alongside this member."
msgstr "- [drawer-layout.content](/api/css/drawer-layout.content.md) — Ko te pane matua e rerekē ana kia hāngai tahi ki tēnei mema."

#: css/file-drop.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: file-drop"
msgstr ""

#: css/file-drop.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`.instui-file-drop` — A file dropzone with hover, accepted, and rejected states."
msgstr "`.instui-file-drop` — He paewhiri tuku kōnae me ngā tūnga whakatā (hover), whakaaetia, me te whakahē."

#: css/file-drop.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The `-hover`/`-accepted`/`-rejected` classes are purely visual — actual drag-and-drop detection and file validation are the consumer's JS to wire up around the wrapped native input."
msgstr "Ko ngā karauna `-hover`/`-accepted`/`-rejected` he mea āhua anake — ko te mōrearea toia-ki-raro tūturu me te whakamana kōnae he mahi JS mā te kaiwhakamahi kia tūhono ki te whakauru taketake kua kapi."

#: css/file-drop.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "**Source:** [file-drop.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/file-drop/file-drop.css)"
msgstr "**Source:** [file-drop.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/file-drop/file-drop.css)"

#: css/file-drop.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Wrap a native `<input type=\"file\">` in the `<label>` drop zone so it stays a real, labelled file control that the keyboard and assistive tech can operate."
msgstr "Kapihia he `<input type=\"file\">` taketake ki roto i te pae taka `<label>` kia noho tonu hei whakahaere kōnae tūturu kua tapaina ka taea te whakahaere e te papapātuhi me ngā taputapu āwhina."

#: css/file-drop.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Drag state for an acceptable file."
msgstr "Tūnga toia-ki-raro mō te kōnae e whakaaetia ana."

#: css/file-drop.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Hover or drag-over state."
msgstr "Tūnga whakatā (hover) rānei toia-ki-raro."

#: css/file-drop.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Render the leading dropzone glyph icon."
msgstr "Whakaaturia te tohu glyph ārahi o te paewhiri taka."

#: css/file-drop.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Drag state for a rejected file."
msgstr "Tūnga toia-ki-raro mō te kōnae kua whakahē."

#: css/form-field-group.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: form-field-group"
msgstr ""

#: css/form-field-group.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`.instui-form-field-group` — A `<fieldset>` group with a legend, a column or inline layout, and configurable spacing."
msgstr "`.instui-form-field-group` — He rōpū `<fieldset>` me tētahi kupu tohu (legend), he whakarite i te tūnga pou rānei te tuinga ā-ipurangi, me ngā wāhi e taea te whakarite."

#: css/form-field-group.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Sets its own `gap` between fields, tunable with the `-col-spacing-*`/`-row-spacing-*` modifiers below — prefer those over chaining a generic `-gap-*` spacing utility modifier, which overrides the built-in value outright."
msgstr "Ka whakarite i tōna ake `gap` i waenga i ngā mara, ka taea te whakarite mā ngā kōwhiringa `-col-spacing-*`/`-row-spacing-*` i raro nei — kia tūpato ki ēnei kaua e whakamahi noa i te hono i tētahi kaiwhakahaere wāhi `-gap-*` whānui, nō te mea ka whakawāteahia te uara ā-roto."

#: css/form-field-group.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "**Source:** [form-field-group.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/form-field-group/form-field-group.css)"
msgstr "**Source:** [form-field-group.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/form-field-group/form-field-group.css)"

#: css/form-field-group.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Renders a native `<fieldset>` with a `<legend>`, so the legend text names the whole group for assistive tech."
msgstr "Ka whakaputa i tētahi `<fieldset>` taketake me tētahi `<legend>`, kia ingoa ai te kuputohu (legend) ki te rōpū katoa mō ngā hangarau āwhina."

#: css/form-field-group.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Large column gap."
msgstr "Wāhi pou nui."

#: css/form-field-group.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Medium column gap."
msgstr "Wāhi pou waenga."

#: css/form-field-group.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "No column gap."
msgstr "Kāore he wāhi pou."

#: css/form-field-group.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Small column gap."
msgstr "Wāhi pou iti."

#: css/form-field-group.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Align child fields to a shared grid."
msgstr "Whakakotahi ngā mara tamaiti ki tētahi gridi tiritahi."

#: css/form-field-group.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Lay child fields out in columns."
msgstr "Whakaritea ngā mara tamaiti kia tau ki roto i ngā pou."

#: css/form-field-group.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Lay child fields inline, in a row."
msgstr "Whakaritea ngā mara tamaiti kia rārangi ā-ipurangi, i tētahi rārangi kotahi."

#: css/form-field-group.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Mark the group as required."
msgstr "Tohua te rōpū hei mea e hiahiatia ana."

#: css/form-field-group.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Large row gap."
msgstr "Wāhi rārangi nui."

#: css/form-field-group.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Medium row gap."
msgstr "Wāhi rārangi waenga."

#: css/form-field-group.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "No row gap."
msgstr "Kāore he wāhi rārangi."

#: css/form-field-group.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Small row gap."
msgstr "Wāhi rārangi iti."

#: css/form-field-group.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Bottom-align the fields."
msgstr "Whakatikahia ngā mara kia rite ki raro."

#: css/form-field-group.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Middle-align the fields."
msgstr "Whakatikahia ngā mara ki waenganui."

#: css/form-field-group.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Top-align the fields."
msgstr "Whakatikahia ngā mara kia eke ki runga."

#: css/form-field-group.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Renders the decorative required-field asterisk after the legend text when the group is required."
msgstr "Ka whakaatu i te whetu asterisk whakapaipai mō te mara hiahiatanga i muri i te tuhinga kupu tohu (legend) mēnā ka hiahiatia te rōpū."

#: css/form-field-group.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- The `-layout-aligned` mode uses CSS subgrid behind an `@supports` guard; where subgrid is unsupported, the fields fall back to their own stacked layout."
msgstr "- Ka whakamahi te aratau `-layout-aligned` i te CSS subgrid i raro i te tiaki `@supports`; mēnā kāore te subgrid e tautokona ana, ka hoki ngā mara ki tō rātou ake whakatakotoranga tūpato (stacked)."

#: css/form-field-group.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- [form-field](/api/css/form-field.md) — The single field this group repeats.\n- [radio-input-group](/api/css/radio-input-group.md) — Groups radio inputs under a legend."
msgstr "- [form-field](/api/css/form-field.md) — Te mara kotahi e tārite ana tēnei rōpū.\n- [radio-input-group](/api/css/radio-input-group.md) — E whakarōpū ana i ngā paatene irirangi (radio inputs) i raro i tētahi kupu tohu."

#: css/form-field-messages.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: form-field-messages"
msgstr ""

#: css/form-field-messages.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`.instui-form-field-messages` — Field help and validation messages — hint, error, success, and screen-reader-only — with a glyph on error and success."
msgstr "`.instui-form-field-messages` — He āwhina ā-pārae me ngā karere whakamana — tohutohu, hapa, angitū, me ngā karere mō ngā kaipānui mata anake — me tētahi tohu whakairo i ngā hapa me ngā angitū."

#: css/form-field-messages.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Sets its own `gap` between stacked messages; chaining a `-gap-*` spacing utility modifier overrides that built-in value."
msgstr "Ka tautuhia tōna ake `gap` i waenganui i ngā karere e rārangi ana; mā te here i tētahi kaiwhakatikatika wāhi `-gap-*` ka whakakapi i taua uara kua hanga."

#: css/form-field-messages.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "**Source:** [form-field-messages.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/form-field-messages/form-field-messages.css)"
msgstr "**Source:** [form-field-messages.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/form-field-messages/form-field-messages.css)"

#: css/form-field-messages.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A `-type-screenreader-only` message is visually hidden but stays in the accessibility tree, so it's still announced; pair error and success messages with the field via aria-describedby so assistive tech reads them with the control."
msgstr "He mea huna ā-ata te karere `-type-screenreader-only` engari ka noho tonu i te rākau urupare, nō reira ka panuitia tonu; whakakotahitia ngā karere hapa me ngā angitū ki te āhua mā te aria-describedby kia pānuitia e ngā taputapu āwhina me te mana whakahaere."

#: css/form-field-messages.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "<span class=\"instui-pill -color-info pantoken-doc-tag\">Alias</span> — maps to `.-type-error`."
msgstr ""

#: css/form-field-messages.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "An individual message; its `-type-*` picks the hint, error, success, or screen-reader-only variant."
msgstr "He karere takitahi; ka kōwhiri tōna `-type-*` i te momo: tohutohu, hapa, angitū, ranei mō ngā kaipānui mata anake."

#: css/form-field-messages.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Renders the leading status glyph on error and success messages: an alert circle for errors and a check circle for success."
msgstr "Ka whakaatu i te tohu āhua tūnga i runga i ngā karere hapa me ngā angitū: he porowhita whakatūpato mō ngā hapa, he porowhita tohu-tika mō te angitū."

#: css/form-field-messages.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- [form-field](/api/css/form-field.md) — Wraps a label, controls, and these messages."
msgstr "- [form-field](/api/css/form-field.md) — Ka kapi i tētahi tapanga, ngā mana whakahaere, me ēnei karere."

#: css/form-field.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: form-field"
msgstr ""

#: css/form-field.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`.instui-form-field` — A form-field wrapper: a label, its controls, and inline, required, or readonly layouts."
msgstr "`.instui-form-field` — He whakakapi-ā-pūnaha ā-wāhanga: he tapanga, āna mana whakahaere, me ngā whakaritenga ā-rārangi, me ngā arataki rānei, kāore e taea te whakatika."

#: css/form-field.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "An error message stays hidden until the field's control is `:user-invalid` (after the user interacts) or you add the `-invalid` class. Use `-layout-inline` to put the label beside the controls and `-layout-stacked` to put it above. Also sets its own `gap` between the label, controls, and messages; chaining a `-gap-*` spacing utility modifier overrides that built-in value."
msgstr "Ka huna te karere hapa kia tae rā anō te mana whakahaere o te wāhanga ki te āhua `:user-invalid` (i muri i te hononga a te kaiwhakamahi) rānei ki te tāpiri koe i te karaehe `-invalid`. Whakamahia te `-layout-inline` ki te whakanoho i te tapanga ki taha o ngā mana whakahaere, ā, te `-layout-stacked` hei whakanoho i runga ake. Ka tautuhi hoki i tana ake `gap` i waenga i te tapanga, ngā mana whakahaere, me ngā karere; mā te here i tētahi kaitohu whakarahi `-gap-*` ka huri i taua uara tūturu."

#: css/form-field.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "**Source:** [form-field.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/form-field/form-field.css)"
msgstr "**Source:** [form-field.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/form-field/form-field.css)"

#: css/form-field.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The `<label>` element wraps the control, so the label text names it natively; the required asterisk is decorative and should be hidden from assistive tech (aria-hidden), and the error message surfaces once the control is `:user-invalid` or you add the `-invalid` class."
msgstr "Ka whakakapi te waahanga `<label>` i te mana whakahaere, nō reira ka tū ingoa taketake te kuputuhi tapanga; he whakapae noa te asteriski e tohu ana he herenga, me huna ia i te hangarau āwhina (aria-hidden), ā, ka puta te karere hapa ka tae te mana whakahaere ki te āhua `:user-invalid` rānei ka tāpirihia te karaehe `-invalid`."

#: css/form-field.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Inline layout (shorthand for `-layout-inline`)."
msgstr "Whakakitenga ā-rārangi (kua poto mō `-layout-inline`)."

#: css/form-field.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "End-align the label text."
msgstr "Whakatika te kuputuhi tapanga ki te mutunga."

#: css/form-field.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Start-align the label text."
msgstr "Whakatika te kuputuhi tapanga ki te tīmatanga."

#: css/form-field.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Inline layout: label beside the controls."
msgstr "Whakakitenga ā-rārangi: tapanga ki taha o ngā mana whakahaere."

#: css/form-field.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Stacked layout: label above the controls."
msgstr "Whakakitenga tūru: tapanga i runga ake i ngā mana whakahaere."

#: css/form-field.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Bottom-align the label with the controls."
msgstr "Whakatika te tapanga kia taurite raro ki ngā mana whakahaere."

#: css/form-field.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Top-align the label with the controls."
msgstr "Whakatika te tapanga kia taurite runga ki ngā mana whakahaere."

#: css/form-field.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The control area beside or below the label."
msgstr "Te wāhi mana whakahaere kei te taha, kei raro rānei o te tapanga."

#: css/form-field.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The field label."
msgstr "Te tapanga wāhanga."

#: css/form-field.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Renders the decorative required-field asterisk after the label text when the field is required."
msgstr "Ka whakaatu i te asteriski whakapaipai e tohu ana he wāhanga taketake i muri i te kuputuhi tapanga ina he mea hiahia te wāhanga."

#: css/form-field.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- [form-field-messages](/api/css/form-field-messages.md) — Renders the field's hint, error, and success messages.\n- [form-field-group](/api/css/form-field-group.md) — Groups related fields under a shared legend."
msgstr "- [form-field-messages](/api/css/form-field-messages.md) — Ka whakaatu i ngā aratohu, ngā hapa, me ngā karere angitu o te wāhanga.\n- [form-field-group](/api/css/form-field-group.md) — Ka rōpū i ngā wāhanga e hāngai ana i raro i tētahi ingoa āheinga tahi."

#: css/gap.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: gap"
msgstr ""

#: css/gap.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`.--gap-md` — Flex/grid `gap` utilities on the spacing scale, short (`--gap-sm`) or long (`--gap-small`) spelling. Usable bare or chained onto any component (`.instui-view.--gap-sm`) — components that already set their own `gap` from a component-specific token may have it overridden."
msgstr "`.--gap-md` — ngā taputapu Flex/grid `gap` i runga i te rārangi wāhenga, he kaituhi poto (`--gap-sm`), he kaituhi roa (`--gap-small`). Ka taea te whakamahi noa, ka honohono rānei ki runga i tētahi kōwae (`.instui-view.--gap-sm`) — ko ngā kōwae e tautuhia kē ana i ō rātou ake `gap` mā tētahi tohu motuhake mō te kōwae, ka taea te whakakapi."

#: css/gap.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "**Source:** [index.ts](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/utilities/gap/index.ts)"
msgstr "**Source:** [index.ts](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/utilities/gap/index.ts)"

#: css/gap.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Applies the medium spacing token as the gap."
msgstr "Ka whakamahia te tohu wāhenga waenganui hei te āputa."

#: css/gap.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Gap utilities across short and long spacing-step spellings."
msgstr "Ngā taputapu āputa mō ngā kaituhi wāhenga poto me te roa."

#: css/heading.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: heading"
msgstr ""

#: css/heading.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`.instui-heading` — Heading typography from `-level-h1` to `-level-h6`."
msgstr "`.instui-heading` — Momotuhi upoko mai i `-level-h1` ki `-level-h6`."

#: css/heading.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The `-variant-*` presets override a `-level-*`'s font-size and font-weight, so combine only one of each family per element."
msgstr "Ka whakakāhore ngā tautuhinga `-variant-*` i te rahi momotuhi me te taumaha momotuhi o tētahi `-level-*`, nō reira kia kotahi anake te whakamahi i ia whanau mō ia tūemi."

#: css/heading.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "**Source:** [heading.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/heading/heading.css)"
msgstr "**Source:** [heading.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/heading/heading.css)"

#: css/heading.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "These classes set the visual level only, so render a real `<h1>`–`<h6>` (or use `role=\"heading\"` with `aria-level`) to convey the heading level."
msgstr "Ko ēnei kara he whakarite noa i te taumata ā-āhua; nō reira whakamahi i tētahi `<h1>`–`<h6>` tūturu (rānei whakamahi `role=\"heading\"` me `aria-level`) kia toi mai te taumata upoko."

#: css/heading.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Add a bottom rule."
msgstr "Tāpiri rārangi raro."

#: css/heading.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Add a top rule."
msgstr "Tāpiri rārangi runga."

#: css/heading.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "AI-accent colour."
msgstr "Tae tohu AI."

#: css/heading.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "(default) Primary colour."
msgstr "(taunoa) Tae matua."

#: css/heading.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "On-dark (primary inverse) colour."
msgstr "Tae mō papamuri pouri (matua inverse)."

#: css/heading.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Secondary (muted) colour."
msgstr "Tae tuarua (kāore e kaha)."

#: css/heading.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Render at the h1 type scale."
msgstr "Whakaatu i te rahi momotuhi h1."

#: css/heading.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Render at the h2 type scale."
msgstr "Whakaatu i te rahi momotuhi h2."

#: css/heading.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Render at the h3 type scale."
msgstr "Whakaatu i te rahi momotuhi h3."

#: css/heading.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Render at the h4 type scale."
msgstr "Whakaatu i te rahi momotuhi h4."

#: css/heading.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Render at the h5 type scale."
msgstr "Whakaatu i te rahi momotuhi h5."

#: css/heading.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Render at the h6 type scale."
msgstr "Whakaatu i te rahi momotuhi h6."

#: css/heading.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Label type preset."
msgstr "Tautuhinga momo tapanga."

#: css/heading.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Mini card-title preset."
msgstr "Tautuhinga taitara kāri iti."

#: css/heading.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Regular card-title preset."
msgstr "Tautuhinga taitara kāri noa."

#: css/heading.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Card section-title preset."
msgstr "Tautuhinga taitara wāhanga kāri."

#: css/heading.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Page-title preset."
msgstr "Tautuhinga taitara whārangi."

#: css/heading.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Section-title preset."
msgstr "Tautuhinga taitara wāhanga."

#: css/heading.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- [text](/api/css/text.md) — Body typography for non-heading text."
msgstr "- [text](/api/css/text.md) — Momotuhi tinana mō ngā tuhinga kāore he upoko."

#: css/hero.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: hero"
msgstr ""

#: css/hero.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`div[class~=\"instui-hero\"]` — Full-width header section with title, subtitle, and optional background image."
msgstr "`div[class~=\"instui-hero\"]` — Wāhanga upoko-whānui me te taitara, te taitara-iti, me te whakaahua papamuri kōwhiringa."

#: css/hero.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "✅ Use Hero when:"
msgstr "✅ Whakamahia te Hero mēnā:"

#: css/hero.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- You need a prominent page header with visual hierarchy\n- The page benefits from a large, eye-catching opening section\n- You want to include background imagery or gradient accents\n🚫 Don't use Hero when:"
msgstr "- Me whai koe i tētahi upoko whārangi tino kitea me te whakarōpūtanga ā-aro\n- Ka whai painga te whārangi i tētahi wāhanga tuwhera nui, e kukume ana i te aro\n- Kei te hiahia koe ki te whakauru whakaahua papamuri, kākahu rānei ā-karakaraka\n🚫 Kaua e whakamahi i te Hero mēnā:"

#: css/hero.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- Building a simple page header — use Page-Layout instead\n- The hero competes with critical content — prioritize readability"
msgstr "- E hanga ana i tētahi upoko whārangi māmā — whakamahia te Page-Layout anō\n- Mēnā ka whakataetae te hero ki ngā ihirangi hira — whakamua te pānui mārama"

#: css/hero.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- Ensure the title is in an `<h1>` tag for semantic structure\n- If using background images, provide sufficient color contrast for text\n- Avoid autoplay on video or animation that could distract from content"
msgstr "- Me noho te taitara i roto i te tapanga `<h1>` mō te hanganga semantika\n- Mēnā e whakamahi ana i ngā whakaahua papamuri, whakarato āhua tae ōrite kia mārama te tuhinga\n- Aukati i te purei-aunoa i ngā ataata, i ngā whakahirahira rānei e whakararuraru ai i te ihirangi"

#: css/hero.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Hero subtitle content"
msgstr "Ihirangi taitara-iti o te Hero"

#: css/hero.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Hero title content"
msgstr "Ihirangi taitara o te Hero"

#: css/hero.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Optional action buttons or links."
msgstr "Pātene mahi ā-kōwhiringa, hono rānei."

#: css/hero.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Optional background layer (image or gradient)."
msgstr "Apa papamuri ā-kōwhiringa (whakaahua, kākahu rānei)."

#: css/hero.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Container for hero text and actions."
msgstr "Ipu mō ngā kuputuhi me ngā mahi o te hero."

#: css/hero.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Optional semi-transparent overlay for text contrast."
msgstr "Papaki haurua-mārama ā-kōwhiringa hei whakapakari i te whakarite kuputuhi."

#: css/hero.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Optional supporting text or description."
msgstr "Tuhinga tautoko ā-kōwhiringa, he whakamārama rānei."

#: css/hero.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Main hero title (typically `<h1>`)."
msgstr "Taitara matua o te hero (noa atu `<h1>`)."

#: css/icon.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: icon"
msgstr ""

#: css/icon.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`.instui-icon` — The icon system: `.instui-icon` sizing plus the shared `-icon-<name>` painter that masks a glyph (in `currentColor`) before any element."
msgstr "`.instui-icon` — Te pūnaha tohu: whakarahi `.instui-icon` me te pentara tāpare ā-roto `-icon-<name>` e āraihia ana i tētahi tohu (i roto i `currentColor`) i mua i tētahi tūemi."

#: css/icon.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "**Source:** [icon.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/utilities/icon/icon.css)"
msgstr "**Source:** [icon.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/utilities/icon/icon.css)"

#: css/icon.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The glyph is decorative, so mark it `aria-hidden=\"true\"`; give it a `role` or label only when the icon conveys meaning on its own."
msgstr "He whakapaipai te tohu, nō reira tāmarka kia `aria-hidden=\"true\"`; homai he `role`, he tapanga rānei anake mēnā ka whakaputa tikanga te tohu i a ia anake."

#: css/icon.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Set the glyph token (`--pantoken-glyph`) and render it via the shared painter (for example `-icon-search`)."
msgstr "Whakatakotoria te tohu glyph (`--pantoken-glyph`) ā, whakaatuhia mā te pentara tāpare ā-roto (hei tauira `-icon-search`)."

#: css/icon.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The glyph itself: a 1em box masked from `--pantoken-glyph` and filled with `currentColor`."
msgstr "Te glyph anō: pouaka 1em kua āraihia mai i `--pantoken-glyph`, ā, kua kīa ki `currentColor`."

#: css/img.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: img"
msgstr ""

#: css/img.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`.instui-img` — A styled `<img>` with display, crop, and effect modifiers that stack."
msgstr "`.instui-img` — He `<img>` ā-tae kua whakaritea me ngā whakarerekētanga whakaaturanga, tapahi, me ngā pānga e whakakotahi ana."

#: css/img.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Effects compose through the shared `--pantoken-img-filter` custom property, so `-with-grayscale` and `-with-blur` can apply together; the `-constrain-*` crop modifiers require the consumer to size the box explicitly."
msgstr "Ka hanga ngā pānga mā te rawa ritenga tuitui `--pantoken-img-filter`, nō reira ka taea e `-with-grayscale` me `-with-blur` te tono tahi; ko ngā whakarerekētanga tapahi `-constrain-*` e tono ana kia whakaritea e te kaiwhakamahi te rahinga o te pouaka."

#: css/img.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "**Source:** [img.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/img/img.css)"
msgstr "**Source:** [img.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/img/img.css)"

#: css/img.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Provide meaningful `alt` text that describes the image, and use an empty `alt=\"\"` for purely decorative images so assistive tech skips them."
msgstr "Whakarato tuhinga `alt` whai tikanga e whakamārama ana i te whakaahua, ā, whakamahia he `alt=\"\"` kore-ihirangi mō ngā whakaahua whakapaipai noa kia whakakorengia ngā taputapu āwhina."

#: css/img.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Scale to fit within the box (contain)."
msgstr "Whakanuia kia uru ki roto i te pouaka (contain)."

#: css/img.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Scale to fill the box (cover)."
msgstr "Whakanuia kia kī i te pouaka (cover)."

#: css/img.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Display as a block element."
msgstr "Whakaaturia hei tūemi poraka."

#: css/img.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Apply a blur effect."
msgstr "Whakamahia he pānga pōhoi (blur)."

#: css/img.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Apply a grayscale effect."
msgstr "Whakamahia he pānga tae-kore (grayscale)."

#: css/img.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "filter &lt;filter-value-list&gt; \\| none — The composed CSS filter on the image; the effect modifiers set it, and you can override it for a custom filter."
msgstr "filter &lt;filter-value-list&gt; \\| none — Te tātari CSS kua whakakotahihia mō te whakaahua; ko ngā whakarerekētanga pānga e tautuhi ana i tēnei, ā, ka taea e koe te huri kia whakamahi i tētahi tātari ritenga."

#: css/in-place-edit.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: in-place-edit"
msgstr ""

#: css/in-place-edit.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`.instui-in-place-edit` — A [contenteditable] that reads as text until focused, then shows input chrome."
msgstr "`.instui-in-place-edit` — He [contenteditable] e pānuitia ana hei kuputuhi kia tae rā anō ki te aro, kātahi ka whakaatu i te atanga whakauru."

#: css/in-place-edit.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The input chrome only appears while focused; `-readonly` suppresses both the hover and focus affordances so the element always reads as plain inline text."
msgstr "Ka puta anake te atanga whakauru i te wā e aro ana; kāore e whakaaetia e `-readonly` ngā āhuatanga hover me te focus, nō reira ka pānuitia tonu te wāhanga hei kuputuhi ā-tīwae noa."

#: css/in-place-edit.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "**Source:** [in-place-edit.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/in-place-edit/in-place-edit.css)"
msgstr "**Source:** [in-place-edit.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/in-place-edit/in-place-edit.css)"

#: css/in-place-edit.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Give the editable element `role=\"textbox\"` and an accessible name (`aria-label`)."
msgstr "Homai ki te wāhanga ka taea te whakatika `role=\"textbox\"` me tētahi ingoa e wātea ana (`aria-label`)."

#: css/in-place-edit.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Shown inline but not editable (no hover/focus affordance)."
msgstr "Whakaaturia ā-tīwae engari kāore e taea te whakatika (kāore he āhuatanga hover/focus)."

#: css/in-place-edit.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "- [text-input](/api/css/text-input.md) — On focus it shows the same input chrome as a text input."
msgstr "- [text-input](/api/css/text-input.md) — I te wā e aro ana ka whakaatu i taua atanga whakauru anō, pēnei i tētahi text input."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS API reference"
msgstr ""

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The CSS API reference covers pantoken's class-based component layer: components, utilities, global rules, and declarations built on the token system."
msgstr "Ko te whakawhānuitanga API CSS e kapi ana i te papa waahanga-kāwai o pantoken: ngā kōwae, ngā taputapu, ngā ture ā-ao, me ngā whakapuakitanga i hangaia i runga i te pūnaha tohu."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "## Components"
msgstr ""

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "Name"
msgstr "Ingoa"

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "Class"
msgstr "Kāwai"

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "Summary"
msgstr "Whakarāpopototanga"

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A surface container for AI agents."
msgstr "He ipu mata mō ngā kaitautoko AI."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "An inline message with a status colour bar and a masked status glyph from the shared icon set."
msgstr "He karere rārangi-iri me tētahi pae tae ā-tūnga me tētahi tohu tūnga āpokapa mai i te kohinga tohu āwhina."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A user avatar showing initials or an image, circular by default."
msgstr "He ātaahua kaiwhakamahi e whakaatu ana i ngā takahuri rānei he whakaahua, porohita mā te taunoa."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A small count or status dot placed over a target's corner."
msgstr "He pūtau tau iti, he piro tūnga rānei i whakatakotoria ki runga i te kokonga o tētahi tūnga."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A dismissible, iconed message surface for page-level or in-context announcements."
msgstr "He mata karere ka taea te whakakore, he tohu hoki, mō ngā pānui taumata whārangi, ā-roanga rānei."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A large empty-state or call-to-action block: a hero icon or image, a heading, and a message."
msgstr "He poraka tūnga-kore nui, he karanga ki te mahi rānei: he tohu ārahi, he taitara, me tētahi karere."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A breadcrumb trail with separators; the last crumb is the current page."
msgstr "He ara pihikete me ngā wehewehe; ko te pihikete whakamutunga ko te whārangi o nāianei."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A crumb (InstUI `Breadcrumb.Link`), an `<li>` in the parent's `<ol>`; the last one is the current page."
msgstr "He pihikete (InstUI `Breadcrumb.Link`), he `<li>` i roto i te `<ol>` matua; ko te mea whakamutunga ko te whārangi o nāianei."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "An accessible action control, styled from the token palette; primary by default."
msgstr "He mana mahi āhei, kua whakatikaina mai i te papa tohu; matua mā te taunoa."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A media object: a hero figure beside a title and description."
msgstr "He tūnga pāpāho: he ahua ārahi i te taha o te taitara me te whakamārama."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A static month grid with navigation, weekday headers, and day cells."
msgstr "He whatunga marama marama marama-marama me te whakatere, ngā upoko rā o ngā rā, me ngā pūtau rā."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A day cell (InstUI `Calendar.Day`); `-today`, `-selected`, and `-outside-month` mark its state."
msgstr "He pūtau rā (InstUI `Calendar.Day`); ko `-today`, `-selected`, me `-outside-month` e tohu ana i tōna āhua."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A surface container that accepts arbitrary content."
msgstr "He ipu mata e āhei ana ki te tūnga ihirangi whānui."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A native checkbox and its label, or a switch via `-variant-toggle`."
msgstr "He pouaka tirotiro mōrearea ā-tūmatanui me tana tūtohu, rānei he pana mā te `-variant-toggle`."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A transparent icon button that draws its own × glyph, in three sizes plus an on-color variant."
msgstr "He pātene tohu kōmaru hāngai e tuhi ana i tana ake tohu ×, i ngā rahi e toru me tētahi rerekētanga ā-tāhua."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "An elevated callout with a caret, positionable on any side; works as a native `[popover]`."
msgstr "He karanga whakanuia me tētahi kaitiaki, ka taea te whakanoho ki tetahi taha; ka mahi hei `[popover]` taketake."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A split layout with a collapsible side tray and a primary scrollable content pane."
msgstr "He whakatakotoranga wehe e whai ana i tētahi papu taha ka taea te kumea, me tētahi matua pane ihirangi whakatere."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The primary content pane that fills remaining space beside the tray."
msgstr "Te pane ihirangi matua e whakakī ana i te wāhi e toe ana i te taha o te papu."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The side panel beside main content, with optional overlay and tray-like surface modifiers."
msgstr "Te pānui taha i te taha o te ihirangi matua, me ngā āhuatanga ā-ōrite pērā i te ārai me te mata rite-papu."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A file dropzone with hover, accepted, and rejected states."
msgstr "He wāhi takai kōnae me ngā āhuatanga pērā i te huri, te whakaaetanga, me ngā āhua whakakore."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A form-field wrapper: a label, its controls, and inline, required, or readonly layouts."
msgstr "He kōpaki mara puka: he taitara, ōna mana, me ngā whakaritenga wā i roto, e hiahiatia ana, rānei e panuitia ana."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A `<fieldset>` group with a legend, a column or inline layout, and configurable spacing."
msgstr "He rōpū `<fieldset>` me te tohu, he whakatakotoranga tīwhiri, raraunga rānei, me ngā waahi wā ka taea te whiriwhiri."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Field help and validation messages — hint, error, success, and screen-reader-only — with a glyph on error and success."
msgstr "Ngā āwhina mara me ngā karere tautuhi — aratohu, pepeha hapa, angitū, me ngā mō tēnei-pārongo-kore — me tētahi tohu i runga i te hapa me te angitū."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Heading typography from `-level-h1` to `-level-h6`."
msgstr "Te kāhua taitara mai i `-level-h1` ki `-level-h6`."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A styled `<img>` with display, crop, and effect modifiers that stack."
msgstr "He `<img>` kua whakatakotoria me ngā whakahaere whakaatu, tapahi, me ngā pānga e piri tata ana."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A [contenteditable] that reads as text until focused, then shows input chrome."
msgstr "He [contenteditable] e pānuitia ana hei kuputuhi kia whanake te aro, kātahi ka whakaatu i te anga urunga."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A facade around a text input with leading and trailing icon slots."
msgstr "He aturanga i runga i te mata mō te kuputuhi me ngā kōwhiringa tohu ā-mua me ā-muri."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A styled hyperlink with sizes, an inverse variant for dark backgrounds, and inline or unstyled forms."
msgstr "He hononga āhua kua whakapaipai me ngā rahi, tētahi rerekētanga urutau mō ngā papamuri pango, ā me ngā āhua ā-rārangi rānei."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A list with token-driven item spacing."
msgstr "He rārangi me te wāhi whakatakoto ā-aitu mā ngā tūemi."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A list item (InstUI `List.Item`)."
msgstr "He tūemi rārangi (InstUI `List.Item`)."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "An in-flow overlay that fills its positioned parent and centres its content — e.g. a spinner over a card. For a modal, prefer a native `<dialog>` (its `::backdrop` is the mask). Every one of these modifiers is also available globally (bare, or chained onto any other component) — see the `mask` global utility."
msgstr "He ārai i roto i-te-taumata e whakakī ana i tana mātua kua whakatakotoria, ka pokapū i ōna ihirangi — hei tauira he poro huri i runga i tētahi kāri. Mō tētahi matapihi matatini, whakamahia he `<dialog>` taketake (ko tana `::backdrop` te wera). Ia kotahi o ēnei pūmotu e wātea ana hoki ā-ao (mā te kore, rānei ka tāpiri ki runga i tētahi atu kīwa) — tirohia te taputapu ā-ao `mask`."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A dropdown surface of items, groups, and separators."
msgstr "He mata taka iho o ngā tūemi, ngā rōpū, me ngā wehewehe."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A labelled group heading (InstUI `Menu.Group`/`Menu.ItemGroup`)."
msgstr "He taitara rōpū ārai — (InstUI `Menu.Group`/`Menu.ItemGroup`)."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A menu entry (InstUI `Menu.Item`); add -disabled, -highlighted, or -active/[aria-checked]."
msgstr "He tomokanga rārangi (InstUI `Menu.Item`); tāpiri -disabled, -highlighted, rānei -active/[aria-checked]."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A divider rule between items (InstUI `Menu.Separator`)."
msgstr "He ture wehe i waenga i ngā tūemi (InstUI `Menu.Separator`)."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A labelled statistic — a large value over a caption."
msgstr "He tatauranga taitara — he uara nui kei runga i tētahi taitara whakarāpopototanga."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A dialog surface (works on a native &lt;dialog&gt;); header/body/footer parts."
msgstr "He mata kōrero (ka mahi i runga i te <dialog> taketake); he wāhanga upoko/tinana/waea."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The content region (InstUI `Modal.Body`); a lone `<img>` goes full-bleed."
msgstr "Te rohe ihirangi (InstUI `Modal.Body`); ka toro-whānui te `<img>` takitahi."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The actions row (InstUI `Modal.Footer`)."
msgstr "Te rārangi mahi (InstUI `Modal.Footer`)."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The title row (InstUI `Modal.Header`)."
msgstr "Te rārangi taitara (InstUI `Modal.Header`)."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A number-input facade with a +/- spinner column."
msgstr "He ārahi tomo-nui me tētahi kōwae +/- mō te poro."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Page navigation: numbered pages, first, previous, next, and last arrows, and an ellipsis for gaps."
msgstr "Te whakatere whārangi: whārangi nama, tuatahi, o mua, ā muri, ā whakamutunga, me te tohu mō ngā wāhi hēkona."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A page link or button (InstUI `Pagination.Page`); the current page carries `[aria-current]`."
msgstr "He hononga whārangi rānei he pātene (InstUI `Pagination.Page`); ko te whārangi o nāianei ka mau i te `[aria-current]`."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A compact status label; add a leading glyph with the shared `-icon-<name>` form."
msgstr "He tapanga tūnga pūkete; tāpiri he tohu ā-mua mā te anga `-icon-<name>` āwhina."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "An elevated surface for a native `[popover]`, positioned with CSS anchor positioning."
msgstr "He mata whakanuia mō te `[popover]` taketake, e whakanohoia ana mā te whakatakoto ā-CSS."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A determinate progress bar with a coloured meter, sizes, and an optional value label."
msgstr "He pae ahunga whakarite me tētahi mita tae, ngā rahi, me tētahi tapanga uara kōwhiringa."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A circular progress ring driven by `--value` and `--value-max` custom properties."
msgstr "He wira ahunga porohita e taraihia ana e ngā āhuatanga ritenga `--value` me `--value-max`."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A native radio button and its label."
msgstr "He pātene reo taketake me tana tūtohu."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A single-select radio `<fieldset>`, plain or as a connected segmented toggle."
msgstr "He rōpū pātene reo kotahi-te-kōwhiri `<fieldset>`, he āhua mārama, he rānei hei pana rēreti hono."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A styled range slider with an inverse value bubble."
msgstr "He rāruraru rārangi whānui kua whakapaipai me te pōkarekare uara whakatika."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A star rating with filled and empty glyphs and an optional numeric label."
msgstr "He reiti whetū me ngā āhuatanga kīhai i whakakīia me ngā wāhi kore-kī, me tētahi tapanga ā-tau kōwhiringa."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A vertical navigation rail of icon-over-label items, with a minimized icons-only mode."
msgstr "He ara whakatere tūāhua poutū o ngā tohu-iti-nui i runga i te tapanga, ā, he aratau iti anake-ngā tohu tāme."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A navigation entry (InstUI `SideNavBar.Item`); `-selected` marks the active one."
msgstr "He tomokanga whakatere (InstUI `SideNavBar.Item`); ka tohu `-selected` i te mea tūnga."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A styled native `<select>` with a caret, matching the text-input states and sizes."
msgstr "He `<select>` taketake kua oti te āhua me tētahi karet, e ōrite ana ki ngā āhuatanga me ngā rahi o te tomokanga kuputuhi."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "An animated loading ring; give it role=\"status\" and an aria-label."
msgstr "He whiringa porowhita kawemai e neke ana; whakamānawa ki a ia te role=\"status\" me tētahi aria-label."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A styled data table for `th` and `td` plus an optional caption, with hover, fixed, and stacked-card layouts."
msgstr "He tēpu raraunga āhua mō `th` me `td` me tētahi taitara kōwhiringa, me ngā whakamahinga paheko, tatau pakari, me ngā aronga kāri weriweri."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The table's data row group (InstUI `Table.Body`)."
msgstr "Ko te rōpū rārangi raraunga o te tēpu (InstUI `Table.Body`)."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A data cell (InstUI `Table.Cell`)."
msgstr "He pūtau raraunga (InstUI `Table.Cell`)."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A column-header cell (InstUI `Table.ColHeader`); the default `th` styling, overridden by `table.row-header` for `th[scope=\"row\"]`."
msgstr "He pūtau taitara-column (InstUI `Table.ColHeader`); ko te āhua taunoa `th` ka tārewahia e `table.row-header` mō `th[scope=\"row\"]`."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The table's header row group (InstUI `Table.Head`)."
msgstr "Ko te rōpū rārangi upoko o te tēpu (InstUI `Table.Head`)."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A table row (InstUI `Table.Row`)."
msgstr "He rārangi tēpu (InstUI `Table.Row`)."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A row-header cell (InstUI `Table.RowHeader`); styled from the row-header tokens, not the column-header ones."
msgstr "He pūtau taitara-rārangi (InstUI `Table.RowHeader`); kua āhuaia nō ngā tohu taitara-rārangi, ehara i ngā tohu taitara-column."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A tabbed panel set: a tab list, selectable tabs, and their panels."
msgstr "He huinga papa rārangi me ripa: rārangi ripa, ripa rānei ka taea te kōwhiri, me ō rātou papa."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The content panel for a tab (InstUI `Tabs.Panel`)."
msgstr "Te papa ihirangi mō tētahi ripa (InstUI `Tabs.Panel`)."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A single tab button (InstUI `Tabs.Tab`, configured via the parent `Tabs`'s tab list); `-selected` marks the active one."
msgstr "He pātene kotahi ripa (InstUI `Tabs.Tab`, kua whirihorahia mā te rārangi ripa o te matua `Tabs`); ka tohu `-selected` i te mea tūnga."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "An inline chip for a keyword or filter."
msgstr "He pihikete ā-rārangi mō tētahi kupu matua, kupu rānei taatari."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Body-text typography with size, weight, colour, and style modifiers."
msgstr "Ngā momo tuhinga ā-tinana mō te kuputuhi tinana me ngā whakarereke rahi, taumaha, tae, me te āhua."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A styled, resizable native `<textarea>` with the same states and sizes as the text input."
msgstr "He `<textarea>` taketake kua āhua, ka taea te whakarahi, me ngā āhuatanga me ngā rahi ōrite ki te tomokanga kuputuhi."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A styled native `<input>` — including `date`, `time`, and `datetime-local`, where the browser supplies the picker — with validation states and sizes."
msgstr "He `<input>` taketake kua āhua — tae atu ki `date`, `time`, me `datetime-local`, ā, ko te pūtirotiro ka tuku i te kaitīpoka — me ngā āhuatanga whakau me ngā rahi."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A styled native `<details>` disclosure with a rotating chevron."
msgstr "He `<details>` taketake kua āhua mō te whakamārama me tētahi pere hurihuri."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A bordered disclosure built on `<details>`: a chevron summary row and collapsible content."
msgstr "He whakamārama pereti ā-papa i hangaia i runga i `<details>`: he rārangi whakarākei pere me te ihirangi takiri."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A CSS hover and focus tooltip bubble, positionable on any side."
msgstr "He puehu kōrero ā-CSS mō te paheko me te aro, e taea ana te tū ki ngā taha katoa."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "An edge-pinned panel that slides in from any side; a native `[popover]` or `<dialog>`."
msgstr "He papa here-iti e pēhia ana ki ngā taha ka taka mai i tētahi taha; he `[popover]` taketake, ā, he `<dialog>` rānei."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A disclosure tree of nested collections and leaf items, with rotating chevrons."
msgstr "He rākau whakamarama o ngā kohinga tārahi me ngā tūemi rauemi, me ngā pere hurihuri."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The View primitive: a neutral box with key-value modifiers for background, border, radius, shadow, display, position, overflow, and cursor. Every one of these modifiers is also available globally (bare, or chained onto any other component) — see the `background`/`border`/`shadow`/`display`/`position`/`overflow`/`cursor` utilities."
msgstr "Ko te pūtau View: he pouaka tūturu me ngā whakarerekētanga matua-uara mō te papamuri, tātai, porohita, atarangi, whakaatu, tūranga, pāpaku, me te kī. Kei ia kotahi o ēnei whakarerekētanga te wāhi ki te taumata ao (mā te whakamahi māori, mena rānei i runga i tētahi atu kōwae) — tirohia ngā taputapu `background`/`border`/`shadow`/`display`/`position`/`overflow`/`cursor`."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "## Utilities"
msgstr ""

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Semantic colour utilities: `.--bg-<name>`, `.--text-<name>` (aliased as `.--color-<name>`), and `.--border-<name>` for the curated semantic palette. Every one of these also has a component-attached alias modifier (for example `-bg-danger` on any `.instui-<component>`)."
msgstr "Ngā taputapu tae ā-āhuatanga: `.--bg-<name>`, `.--text-<name>` (kua ingoa-iritia hei `.--color-<name>`), me `.--border-<name>` mō te rārangi tae ā-āhua kua whakaritea. Kei ia o ēnei he ingoa-taapiri honohono ā-kōwae (hei tauira `-bg-danger` i runga i tētahi `.instui-<component>`)."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`cursor` as a composable, global class — `.--cursor-<value>` — usable bare or chained onto any component (`.instui-button.--cursor-pointer`)."
msgstr "`cursor` hei karaehe whakakotahi, ā-ao — `.--cursor-<value>` — ka taea te whakamahi ā-kore, ā-rārangi rānei ki runga i tētahi kōwae (`.instui-button.--cursor-pointer`)."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Flex/grid `gap` utilities on the spacing scale, short (`--gap-sm`) or long (`--gap-small`) spelling. Usable bare or chained onto any component (`.instui-view.--gap-sm`) — components that already set their own `gap` from a component-specific token may have it overridden."
msgstr "Ngā taputapu Flex/grid `gap` i runga i te taera wāhanga, ā, kupu poto (`--gap-sm`) rānei roa (`--gap-small`). Ka taea te whakamahi ā-kore, ā-rārangi rānei ki runga i tētahi kōwae (`.instui-view.--gap-sm`) — ko ngā kōwae e tautuhi ana i ā rātou ake `gap` mai i tētahi tohu ā-kōwae ka āhei pea te whakakapi."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The icon system: `.instui-icon` sizing plus the shared `-icon-<name>` painter that masks a glyph (in `currentColor`) before any element."
msgstr "Te pūnaha ā-tahua: te āhua whakatau `.instui-icon` ā-taimana me te peita tohatoha `-icon-<name>` e whakamask i tētahi tohu (i roto i `currentColor`) i mua i tētahi wāhanga."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Display and text-align utilities — `.--display-<value>` and `.--text-align-<value>` — as composable, global classes, usable bare or chained onto any component."
msgstr "Ngā taputapu whakaatu me te whakatikatika-kuputuhi — `.--display-<value>` me `.--text-align-<value>` — hei karaehe whakakotahi, ā-ao, ka taea te whakamahi ā-kore, ā-rārangi rānei ki runga i tētahi kōwae."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A global, dual copy of the `mask` component's overlay modifiers — `--mask-overlay`, `--mask-fullscreen`, `--mask-blur` — usable bare or chained onto any component, without wrapping in a `.instui-mask` element."
msgstr "He kape ā-ao, rua o ngā whakarerekētanga kopae o te kōwae `mask` — `--mask-overlay`, `--mask-fullscreen`, `--mask-blur` — ka taea te whakamahi ā-kore, ā-rārangi rānei ki runga i tētahi kōwae, me te kore e whakakapi i roto i tētahi tūemi `.instui-mask`."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`overflow-x`/`overflow-y` as composable, global classes — `.--overflow-x-<value>` / `.--overflow-y-<value>` — usable bare or chained onto any component."
msgstr "`overflow-x`/`overflow-y` hei karaehe whakakotahi, ā-ao — `.--overflow-x-<value>` / `.--overflow-y-<value>` — ka taea te whakamahi ā-kore, ā-rārangi rānei ki runga i tētahi kōwae."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`position` as a composable, global class — `.--position-<value>` — usable bare or chained onto any component (`.instui-button.--position-relative`)."
msgstr "`position` hei karaehe whakakotahi, ā-ao — `.--position-<value>` — ka taea te whakamahi ā-kore, ā-rārangi rānei ki runga i tētahi kōwae (`.instui-button.--position-relative`)."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Viewport- or container-width show/hide classes across a themed breakpoint scale."
msgstr "Ngā karaehe whakaatu/ huna whānui mō te whanui tirohanga, rānei te whanui ipu, puta noa i tētahi tere-matua kaupapa."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Visually hides content while keeping it available to assistive tech (the standard clip pattern)."
msgstr "E huna ana i te tirohanga, engari ka pupuri tonu i te wāhi mō ngā taputapu āwhina (te tauira paera tapahi)."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Margin and padding utilities — `.--m<side>-<step>` / `.--margin-<side>-<step>` and `.--p<side>-<step>` / `.--padding-<side>-<step>` on the spacing scale (sides `t`/`b`/`s`/`e`/`x`/`y` or none, spelled short or fully long — for example `--mb-sm` and `--margin-bottom-small` are the same rule; margin also takes `auto`). Usable bare or chained onto any component (for example `class=\"instui-view --mb-sm\"`)."
msgstr "Ngā taputapu margin me padding — `.--m<side>-<step>` / `.--margin-<side>-<step>` me `.--p<side>-<step>` / `.--padding-<side>-<step>` i runga i te paiāwhina mokowā (ngā taha `t`/`b`/`s`/`e`/`x`/`y` rānei kāore, āpitihia hei poto, hei roa rānei — hei tauira `--mb-sm` me `--margin-bottom-small` he ture kotahi; ka taea hoki te whakamahi i te margin ki `auto`). Ka taea te whakamahi mokemoke, mokowhiti rānei hei taurite ki tētahi wāhanga (hei tauira `class=\"instui-view --mb-sm\"`)."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "z-index depth utilities — `.--stack-<level>` (`deepest`, `below`, `above`, `topmost`) — usable bare or chained onto any component, so layers stack predictably instead of by hand-tuned numbers."
msgstr "Ngā taputapu hohonu z-index — `.--stack-<level>` (`deepest`, `below`, `above`, `topmost`) — ka taea te whakamahi mokemoke, mokowhiti rānei ki tētahi wāhanga, kia whāriki ngā papa i runga i te tikanga, kaua e rīpenehia ki ngā nama ā-ringa."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Animation state classes for the `Transition` component — `.instui-transition` and state classes (`-transition-fade-entering`, `-transition-scale-exited`, etc.) — usable bare or chained onto any component."
msgstr "Ngā kara ā-kāhua animation mō te wāhanga `Transition` — `.instui-transition` me ērā atu kara ā-kāhua ā-huringa (`-transition-fade-entering`, `-transition-scale-exited`, etc.) — ka taea te whakamahi mokemoke, mokowhiti rānei ki tētahi wāhanga."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Ellipsis truncation with line clamping controlled by `--lines` — usable bare or chained onto any component (`.instui-button.--truncate`)."
msgstr "Whakatewhatewha ellipsis me te whakawātea rārangi mā te `--lines` — ka taea te whakamahi mokemoke, mokowhiti rānei ki tētahi wāhanga (`.instui-button.--truncate`)."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "A layout-debugging outline: compound `.-with-visual-debug` onto any element to outline the box and its immediate children, so a layout's structure is visible at a glance."
msgstr "Tētahi anga whakamātau tatauranga: whakapirihia te `.-with-visual-debug` ki runga i tētahi tūemi kia whakaatu ai i te pouaka me ōna tamariki tonu, kia kitea te hanganga whakatakotoranga i runga i te titiro."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "## Rules"
msgstr ""

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The opt-in global reset: `box-sizing`, the page surface, base text colour and font, `color-scheme`, and link defaults."
msgstr "Te whakahoki ā-motu kōwhiri: `box-sizing`, te mata whārangi, tae kuputuhi tūāpapa me te tohu momotuhi, `color-scheme`, me ngā tautuhinga hono taunoa."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Typographic defaults for raw HTML — headings, paragraphs, lists, links, and code — applied automatically wherever it's imported (default `:where(body)`); pass `options.scope` to target a different content root instead (e.g. `.vp-doc`)."
msgstr "Ngā tūtohu ā-tārua mō HTML mata — ārahi, parakaraka, rārangi, hononga, me te waehere — ka whakamahia aunoa i ngā wā katoa e kawemai ana (taunoa `:where(body)`); tukua `options.scope` hei tohu i tētahi pūtake ihirangi kē (hei tauira `.vp-doc`)."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "## Plugins"
msgstr ""

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Instructure product logos as CSS image tokens: `--instui-logo-<product>-<layout>-<mode>` holds a data-URI SVG, so a logo paints via e.g. `background-image: var(--instui-logo-canvas-horizontal-color)`."
msgstr "Ngā tohu ingoa hua Instructure hei token whakaahua CSS: kei roto i `--instui-logo-<product>-<layout>-<mode>` te SVG data-URI, nō reira ka peitahia tētahi tohu mā te whakamahi pērā i `background-image: var(--instui-logo-canvas-horizontal-color)`."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Opt-in utility classes for the raw primitive palette: `.instui-bg-`/`fg-`/`border-primitive-color-<name>` paint a colour from the primitive colour tokens, plus `font-family`/`font-weight` utilities for the primitive font tokens. Kept out of the semantic utilities so overrides there stay semantic-only."
msgstr "Ngā kara ā-utu kōwhiri mō te papamuri taketake mata: `.instui-bg-`/`fg-`/`border-primitive-color-<name>` ka peita i tētahi tae mai i ngā token tae taketake, me ngā taputapu `font-family`/`font-weight` mō ngā token momotuhi taketake. Kua waiho hē ō rātou ki waho i ngā taputapu aronga kia noho anake hei whakakapi aronga ki reira."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "## layout"
msgstr ""

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Inline information alert for a short reminder or note."
msgstr "He pānui mōhiohio ā-ipurangi hei whakamahara poto, hei tuhipoka rānei."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Full-width header section with title, subtitle, and optional background image."
msgstr "Wāhanga upoko whānui-whānui me te taitara, tāpiri haurua-taitara, me te whakaahua papamuri kōwhiringa."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Standard three-column page layout with header, sidebar, and main content."
msgstr "Hoahoanga whārangi paerewa-toru-column me te upoko, taha taha, me te tūāpapa matua."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Structured note with rubric categories and scoring indicators."
msgstr "Tuhinga ā-tuhituhi kua whakaraupapahia me ngā kāwai rubrica me ngā tohu tohu."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Quote or testimonial display with attribution and optional imagery."
msgstr "Whakaaturanga whakatairanga, kīanga rānei me te tohua me te whakaahua kōwhiringa."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Two-column layout with left and right content regions."
msgstr "Hoahoanga rua-koluma me ngā rohe ihirangi mauī me matau."

#: css/index.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "App-shell row: side nav, container with header, and optional panel."
msgstr "Rārangi anga taupānga: tahuhu taha, ipu me te upoko, me tētahi panui kōwhiringa."

#: css/input-group.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# CSS: input-group"
msgstr ""

#: css/input-group.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "`.instui-input-group` — A facade around a text input with leading and trailing icon slots."
msgstr "`.instui-input-group` — He mata i te tomanga kuputuhi me ngā mokowā tohu i mua me muri."

#: css/input-group.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Wraps the same field chrome as `text-input` with icon slots either side of it; `-should-not-wrap` is only needed when the group's contents would otherwise overflow onto a second line."
msgstr "Ka piri i te āhua o te mara pēnei i `text-input` me ngā mokowā tohu i ngā taha; he mea hiahiatia anake `-should-not-wrap` mēnā ka puta te ihirangi o te rōpū ki tētahi rārangi tuarua."

#: css/input-group.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "**Source:** [input-group.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/input-group/input-group.css)"
msgstr "**Source:** [input-group.css](https://github.com/thedannywahl/pantoken/blob/main/formats/components/src/components/input-group/input-group.css)"

#: css/input-group.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Disabled state."
msgstr "Āhua kua monokia."

#: css/input-group.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Keep the group on one line (no wrapping)."
msgstr "Puritia te rōpū i runga i tētahi rārangi kotahi (kaua e whakawā)."

#: css/input-group.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Success (valid) state."
msgstr "Āhua angitu (tika)."

