msgctxt "docs.api:text"
msgid "# Function: globalModifierSelector()"
msgstr "# Mahi: globalModifierSelector()"

#: packages/utils/src/functions/globalModifierSelector.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Build a global-utility modifier selector: `:where(*).--name.--name.--name`. The modifier class\nrepeated 3x gives the rule (0,3,0) specificity, which deterministically outranks any real 2-class\ncomponent-modifier compound (`.instui-view.-mod`, 0,2,0) regardless of source order — the `:where(*)`\nwrapper contributes zero specificity of its own, so it's purely documentation that this is a global\nmodifier, not a scoping condition. A plain class selector already matches standalone (`--mt-lg` with\nno other class) or chained onto any component, core or plugin-authored, with no per-component\nenumeration needed. Replaces the old bare-class-plus-enumerated-per-component-compound pattern\n(`globalSelectors`/`chainTargets`), which couldn't reach plugin-authored components and didn't scale\nto high-cardinality utilities like spacing."
msgstr "Hangaia he kaiwhiri kaiwhakauru ā-ao mō ngā taputapu: `:where(*).--name.--name.--name`. Mā te whakahōputu karamu ā-ika i te 3 ngā wā ka whiwhi te ture ake (0,3,0) mō te motuhēhēnga, ā, ka whakataetae ia i ngā pūkete pūmau-rua o ngā wāhanga ā-kamupene-me-te-āhuatanga (`.instui-view.-mod`, 0,2,0) ahakoa te raupapa kōrero — kāore he kōrero motuhēhēnga ka tāpiri te hopanga `:where(*)`, nō reira he tuhinga anake hei tohu koinei he kaiwhiri ā-ao, ehara i tētahi āwhina wāhi. Ka ōrite hoki te kaiwhiri karauna noa mō te tū takitahi (`--mt-lg` me te kore ā-karauna anō) rānei ka honoa ki tētahi wāhanga kē, ahakoa nō te pūtake matua, pūrere rānei, ā, kāore he rārangi mō ia wāhanga e hiahiatia. Ka whakakapi i te tauira tawhito o te karauna-mokowā-mārū me te rārangi ia-wāhanga (`globalSelectors`/`chainTargets`), kāore i taea e taua tauira te toro ki ngā wāhanga i tuhia e ngā pūrere, ā, kāore i taea te piki ki ngā taputapu whai maha pēnei i te whakatakoto mokowā."

