msgid "# Function: onColor()"
msgstr "# Mahi: onColor()"

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/functions/onColor.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "The readable foreground — black or white — for content placed *on* `surface`. This is the CSS-only\nform of InstUI's recurring `*-on-color` variants (a focus ring on a brand button, a\nprimary-inverse button's text, an icon on a coloured surface): rather than a fixed inverse token,\nit picks the contrast from the surface itself, so it stays correct as the surface changes."
msgstr "Ko te mata kua pānuitia — pango, mā rānei — mō te ihirangi e tu *ki runga i* `surface`. He momo CSS-anake tēnei o ngā rerekētanga `*-on-color` a InstUI e puta ana auau (he rīngi arotahi i runga i tētahi pātene waitohu, te kuputuhi o te pātene matua-ā-roto, he tohu i runga i tētahi mata tae): kaua e whakamau ki tētahi tohu inverse pūmau, ka tāpae i te wherikotanga mai i te mata ake, kia tika tonu i te panonitanga o te mata."

#: plugins/pantoken/colors/src/functions/onColor.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "It reads the surface's OKLCH lightness through relative color syntax and snaps it to `0` (black) or\n`1` (white) at `threshold` using the `calc(… * infinity)` clamp trick — no JS, no fixed hex."
msgstr "Ka pānui i te ātaahua marama OKLCH o te mata mā te whakamahinga o te pānui tae ā-āhua ka whakatika ia ki `0` (pango) rānei `1` (mā) i te taumata `threshold` mā te tikanga `calc(… * infinity)` clamp — kāore he JS, kāhore he hex pūmau."

