msgstr "### outputWatchPaths?"

#: plugins/vite/workspace-orchestrator/src/interfaces/OrchestratorOptions.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Paths to watch with native `fs.watch` so Vite picks up built output after an upstream rebuild\n(e.g. a package's `dist` or `generated` directory). Uses native `fs.watch` rather than\nchokidar's `add()`, which doesn't reliably detect changes in pnpm-symlinked or out-of-root\ndirectories. On each change a synthetic `\"change\"` event is emitted on `server.watcher`: for\nCSS files already in the module graph Vite triggers a targeted hot-update; for anything else\nit falls back to a full page reload."
msgstr "Ngā ara hei mataara mā te native `fs.watch` kia taea e Vite te tiki i ngā putanga kua hanga i muri i te hanga anō tukuake (hei tauira: te kōpaki `dist` rānei `generated` o tētahi kete). Ka whakamahi i te native `fs.watch` hei utu i te `add()` o chokidar, nā te mea kāore taua mea e kitea ngā panoni i ngā kōpaki kua hono mā pnpm (pnpm-symlinked) me ngā kōpaki kei waho o te pakiaka i runga i te whakahaere. I ia panoni ka whakaputa he kaupapa tāruarua `\"change\"` ki runga i `server.watcher`: mō ngā kōnae CSS kua kei te module graph ka whakaoho a Vite i tētahi hot-update ātaahua; mō ētahi atu katoa ka hoki ki te whakahou whānui o te whārangi."

