msgid "Define the locale subset your app supports. Pass the imported bundle objects as an object\nwhose keys are the locale tags (JavaScript shorthand makes this natural). TypeScript narrows\nthe accepted locale tags to only the keys you provide."
msgstr "Whakaritehia te hauraro reo (locale) e tautokohia ana e tō taupānga. Tāpaehia ngā kohinga kua kawemai hei taonga (object) \nā ngā kī ko ngā tapanga reo (locale tags) (he māmā tēnei mā te whakarapopototanga o JavaScript). Ka whakatatahia e TypeScript \ngā tapanga reo e whakaaetia ana kia noho ki ngā kī anake kua whakarato koe."

#: renderers/web-components/src/functions/createLocaleSet.md
#, no-c-format
msgctxt "docs.api:prose"
msgid "Not calling `createLocaleSet` at all gives the full 44-locale barrel — use this factory only\nwhen you need compile-time validation or explicit tree-shaking signals."
msgstr "Ki te kore rawa e karangahia `createLocaleSet` ka riro te pae katoa o ngā reo e 44 — whakamahia tēnei factory anake \nina hiahia koe i te whakamana i te wā tāpae (compile-time validation) rānei i ngā tohu tangohanga-rākau tūtohu (explicit tree-shaking signals)."

